Privacy Policy
App: Cult AI  |  Developer: Rahul Gornale
Effective date: November 7, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how Rahul Gornale (“we”, “us”, “our”) collects, uses, and protects information when you use the Cult AI mobile application (the “App”) available on Google Play. By using the App, you agree to the practices described here.

1. Information We Collect
Information you provide: This may include your email address and basic account details if you sign in, and the text, prompts, or other content you enter into the App to use its AI features.

Information collected automatically: Device model, operating system version, app version, language settings, crash logs and diagnostics, and your IP address.

Health data: If you grant permission, the App may access health and fitness data from your device or Health Connect, as described in Section 3.

Permissions: The App may request permissions such as internet access and notifications. Any permission is used only for the feature you choose to use, and you can revoke it at any time in your device settings.

2. How We Use Information
To provide, operate, and maintain the App and its AI features
To process your prompts and generate responses
To improve performance, fix bugs, and develop new features
To respond to your support requests
To detect and prevent fraud, abuse, and security issues
To comply with legal obligations
3. Health Data
With your explicit permission, the App may access health and fitness data on your device, including through Android Health Connect. The types of health data the App may access are: [e.g., steps, heart rate, sleep, weight, exercise sessions, nutrition].

How we use it: We use this data only to provide the health and wellness features you choose in the App, such as showing your activity summaries and giving personalized insights. We do not use health data for advertising, and we do not sell it.

Sharing: We do not share health data with third parties except (a) with AI processing providers when you ask the App to analyze your data, only to generate your result and under confidentiality obligations; (b) when required by law; or (c) with your consent. Health data is not used to determine credit, eligibility, or insurance.

Your control: Access is requested only when you use a related feature. You can review or revoke access at any time in Android Settings or the Health Connect app, and you can request deletion of any health data we store by emailing rahulgornale1996@gmail.com. The App is not a medical device and does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment.

4. AI Processing and Third-Party Services
To generate responses, the content you submit in the App is sent to third-party AI model providers and cloud services that process it on our behalf. Please do not enter passwords or financial details into the App. The App may also use the following services, which operate under their own privacy policies:

Google Play Services
Firebase (Analytics, Crashlytics, Authentication)
Third-party AI model providers used to generate responses
5. Sharing of Information
We do not sell your personal information. We share information only with: (a) service providers, including AI model and cloud providers, who help us operate the App; (b) when required by law or to protect rights, safety, or property; and (c) in connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets, with notice to you.

6. Data Retention and Deletion
We keep your information only as long as needed for the purposes above or as required by law. You may request deletion of your data and account at any time by emailing rahulgornale1996@gmail.com with the subject “Delete my data”. We will process verified requests within 30 days.

7. Data Security
We use reasonable technical and organizational measures, including encryption in transit, to protect your information. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.

8. Your Rights and Choices
Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or export your data, and to object to or restrict certain processing. To exercise these rights, contact us at the email below.

9. Children’s Privacy
The App is not directed to children under 13 (or the applicable age in your country), and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them. If you believe a child has provided us personal information, contact us and we will delete it promptly.

10. International Data Transfers
Your information may be processed in countries other than your own, including where our service providers operate. We take steps to ensure appropriate safeguards are in place.

